1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,603
Is Mount Everest really the tallest mountain

2
00:00:02,603 --> 00:00:03,136
on Earth?

3
00:00:03,486 --> 00:00:06,605
Everest's summit is eight thousand eight hundred

4
00:00:06,605 --> 00:00:09,530
forty-nine meters above sea level. Nothing on

5
00:00:09,530 --> 00:00:11,934
Earth reaches higher above the ocean.

6
00:00:12,284 --> 00:00:14,635
But sea level isn't the only way

7
00:00:14,635 --> 00:00:17,428
to measure a mountain. Meet Mauna Kea,

8
00:00:17,428 --> 00:00:18,897
a volcano in Hawaii.

9
00:00:19,247 --> 00:00:21,732
Above the water, it's only about four

10
00:00:21,732 --> 00:00:24,552
thousand two hundred meters tall. But most

11
00:00:24,552 --> 00:00:26,835
of it is hidden under the Pacific.

12
00:00:26,835 --> 00:00:29,051
Measured from its base on the sea

13
00:00:29,051 --> 00:00:31,267
floor, Mauna Kea is more than ten

14
00:00:31,267 --> 00:00:34,289
thousand meters tall, over a kilometer taller

15
00:00:34,289 --> 00:00:35,162
than Everest.

16
00:00:35,512 --> 00:00:38,401
And then there's Chimborazo, a volcano in

17
00:00:38,401 --> 00:00:41,430
Ecuador. It's only six thousand two hundred

18
00:00:41,430 --> 00:00:43,896
sixty-three meters above sea level.

19
00:00:44,246 --> 00:00:46,651
But Earth isn't a perfect ball. It

20
00:00:46,651 --> 00:00:49,410
spins, so it bulges around the equator,

21
00:00:49,410 --> 00:00:52,948
about forty-three kilometers wider there than from

22
00:00:52,948 --> 00:00:53,867
pole to pole.

23
00:00:54,217 --> 00:00:56,926
Chimborazo sits almost on the equator, on

24
00:00:56,926 --> 00:00:59,040
top of that bulge. So its summit

25
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:01,352
is the point on Earth farthest from

26
00:01:01,352 --> 00:01:04,589
the planet's center, about two kilometers farther

27
00:01:04,589 --> 00:01:05,844
out than Everest's.

28
00:01:06,194 --> 00:01:08,903
That means standing on Chimborazo, you're the

29
00:01:08,903 --> 00:01:10,829
closest you can get to the stars

30
00:01:10,829 --> 00:01:12,274
while standing on Earth.

31
00:01:12,624 --> 00:01:15,460
There's even a fourth contender. Denali in

32
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:17,755
Alaska rises about five and a half

33
00:01:17,755 --> 00:01:20,659
kilometers from its base on the surrounding

34
00:01:20,659 --> 00:01:23,157
land, a bigger rise than Everest from

35
00:01:23,157 --> 00:01:25,317
its base on the Tibetan Plateau.

36
00:01:25,667 --> 00:01:28,270
And Everest is still growing, by about

37
00:01:28,270 --> 00:01:30,941
four millimeters a year, as India keeps

38
00:01:30,941 --> 00:01:32,174
pushing into Asia.

39
00:01:32,524 --> 00:01:34,650
Mauna Kea's summit is so high and

40
00:01:34,650 --> 00:01:36,647
clear that it's home to some of

41
00:01:36,647 --> 00:01:39,095
the world's most important telescopes.

42
00:01:39,445 --> 00:01:41,776
So which one is the real tallest?

43
00:01:41,776 --> 00:01:44,672
Everest, Mauna Kea or Chimborazo? Tell me

44
00:01:44,672 --> 00:01:45,802
in the comments.

